% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the names of materials, in the words of the tariff. Fibre names (the
% fibre-name laws of the European Union and the United States, US Customs'
% list of trade names) and the names and abbreviations of plastics (the
% tariff's Chapter 39, US Customs rulings). Bridges.
%
% A name that is both a fibre and a plastic ("acrylic", "nylon") is read as a
% plastic only for a good that is not a textile article.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the polymer of *a good* is *a polymer*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* names the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the textile material *a material*.
    *a name* is a word for the polymer *a polymer*.
    *a name* is a word for plastics.
    *a good* is a textile article.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.
    the cut of *a garment* indicates *a gender*.
    the polymer of *a good* is *a polymer*.
    *a thing* is made of plastics.

the knowledge base materials background includes:

the fibre names regulation is published at "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2011/1007/oj".
the text of the fibre names regulation is at "../sources/eu/reg_1007_2011.txt".
the textile labelling guide is published at "https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/threading-your-way-through-labeling-requirements-under-textile-wool-acts".
the text of the textile labelling guide is at "../sources/ftc/threading_your_way.txt".
the fiber trade names publication is published at "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/rulings/informed-compliance-publications".
the text of the fiber trade names publication is at "../sources/cbp_icp/fiber_trade_names.txt".
HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2039".
the text of HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is at "../sources/hts/chapter_39.txt".
ruling NY N309957 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N309957".
the text of ruling NY N309957 is at "../sources/cbp/N309957.txt".
ruling NY N362334 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N362334".
the text of ruling NY N362334 is at "../sources/cbp/N362334.txt".
ruling NY N334557 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N334557".
the text of ruling NY N334557 is at "../sources/cbp/N334557.txt".

% Fibre names
"polyester" is a word for the textile material polyester,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "polyester".
"cotton" is a word for the textile material cotton,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "cotton".
"wool" is a word for the textile material wool,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "wool".
"acrylic" is a word for the textile material acrylic,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "acrylic".
"nylon" is a word for the textile material nylon,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "polyamide or nylon".
"polyamide" is a word for the textile material polyamide,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "polyamide or nylon".
"elastane" is a word for the textile material elastane,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "elastane".
"spandex" is a word for the textile material spandex,
    as stated in the textile labelling guide, confer "the ISO standard uses the name viscose for the predominant form of rayon, and elastane for spandex".
"viscose" is a word for the textile material viscose,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "viscose".
"rayon" is a word for the textile material rayon,
    as stated in the textile labelling guide, confer "the ISO standard uses the name viscose for the predominant form of rayon".
"modal" is a word for the textile material modal,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "modal".
"lyocell" is a word for the textile material lyocell,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "lyocell".
"silk" is a word for the textile material silk,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "silk".
"linen" is a word for the textile material linen,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "linen".
"cashmere" is a word for the textile material cashmere,
    as stated in the fibre names regulation, confer "cashmere".
"lycra" is a word for the textile material elastane,
    as stated in the fiber trade names publication, confer "Lycra*......................... Elastane".
"dacron" is a word for the textile material polyester,
    as stated in the fiber trade names publication, confer "Dacron* ...................... Polyester".
"tencel" is a word for the textile material lyocell,
    as stated in the fiber trade names publication, confer "Tencel*....................... Lyocell".

% Plastics: the tariff's own names and abbreviations, and rulings
"plastic" is a word for plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914".
"plastics" is a word for plastics,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914".
"pvc" is a word for the polymer polyvinyl chloride,
    as stated in ruling NY N309957, confer "polyvinyl chloride (PVC)".
"pp" is a word for the polymer polypropylene,
    as stated in ruling NY N362334, confer "polypropylene (PP)".
"polypropylene" is a word for the polymer polypropylene,
    as stated in ruling NY N362334, confer "polypropylene (PP)".
"abs" is a word for the polymer acrylonitrile-butadiene-styrene copolymer,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Acrylonitrile-butadiene-styrene (ABS) copolymers".
"pet" is a word for the polymer polyethylene terephthalate,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "polyethylene terephthalate (PET)".
"tpu" is a word for the polymer polyurethane,
    as stated in ruling NY N334557, confer "thermoplastic polyurethane (TPU)".
"polyurethane" is a word for the polymer polyurethane,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polyurethanes".
"silicone" is a word for the polymer silicone,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Silicones (heading 3910)".
"polycarbonate" is a word for the polymer polycarbonate,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polycarbonates".
"polystyrene" is a word for the polymer polystyrene,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polystyrene".
"polyethylene" is a word for the polymer polyethylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polymers of ethylene, in primary forms".
"ptfe" is a word for the polymer polytetrafluoroethylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) resins".
"acrylic" is a word for the polymer acrylic polymer,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Acrylic polymers in primary forms".
"nylon" is a word for the polymer polyamide,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polyamides in primary forms".

rule textile_by_construction with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "does not apply to materials regarded as textile materials of Section XI":
a good is a textile article
    if the fabric construction of the good is a construction.

rule textile_by_cut with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "does not apply to materials regarded as textile materials of Section XI":
a good is a textile article
    if the cut of the good indicates a gender.

rule polymer_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
the polymer of a good is a polymer
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for the polymer the polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

rule plastics_by_polymer with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a good is made of plastics
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for the polymer a polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

rule plastics_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a good is made of plastics
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

scenario case is:
    case names the material "pvc".
    shirt names the material "acrylic".
    the cut of shirt indicates women.
    the fabric construction of scarf is woven.
    scarf names the material "nylon".
    bead names the material "acrylic".
    polymers expects answers ["the polymer of case is polyvinyl chloride", "the polymer of bead is acrylic polymer"].
    plastics expects answers ["case is made of plastics", "bead is made of plastics"].
    fibres expects answers ["lycra is a word for the textile material elastane"].

query polymers is:
    the polymer of which good is which polymer.

query plastics is:
    which thing is made of plastics.

query fibres is:
    "lycra" is a word for the textile material which material.
